**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** How a lab file is laid out and what its columns hold, as the closed sets an import profile is made of (001 §K 'Column-mapping import wizard: sniff the delimiter, header and BOM, and show a preview; map columns to scan variable(s) (unit; raw dial vs physical), signal, σ, timestamp, capture index, experiment key — or to Mueller elements m00…m33 plus configuration columns'; the S9.2 brief; AGENTS.md: a closed set's disk tag is an int, 1-based, read back by `tryOfWire`, and case names take two words). Nothing reads them before step 299. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`: `ImportProfileName` (step 291) moves, its members unchanged, from after `DataAttachmentStatus` to directly before `NamingTemplate` (step 267), so that the kit file can hold profiles (step 299); `DataRowKey`, `DataRowSelection` and `MappedAttachment` stay where step 291 put them. It gains `static member phoneRoiCsv : ImportProfileName` = `Phone ROI CSV` (the profile over `MuellerDataStore.fs:parseMuellerCsv`) and `static member muellerObservations : ImportProfileName` = `Mueller-matrix observations` (the observation file, step 301), each the one place its text is written, and `static member builtIns : ImportProfileName list`, the four built-in names in the order `intensitySeries`, `ellipsometricSeries`, `phoneRoiCsv`, `muellerObservations`. (2) Directly after `ImportProfileName`, five fieldless unions, each with `member this.value : int` (its disk tag, 1 to n in case order), `static member tryOfWire (tag : int) : <the union> option` (`None` for any other tag), `member this.text : string` and `static member all : <the union> list` (the cases in tag order): (a) `DataDelimiter` = `CommaDelimiter` | `SemicolonDelimiter` | `TabDelimiter`, the character between a row's cells, texts `comma`, `semicolon` and `tab`, with `member this.character : char` answering `,`, `;` and the tab character; (b) `HeaderRowChoice` = `HeaderOnFirstRow` | `NoHeaderRow`, whether the first row names the columns, texts `first row is a header` and `no header row`; (c) `ByteOrderMark` = `ByteOrderMarkPresent` | `ByteOrderMarkAbsent`, whether the lab's files start with the UTF-8 byte-order mark, texts `byte-order mark` and `no byte-order mark`: the kit drops a leading mark before anything reads a file (step 128), so the profile records it for the wizard (step 309) and for the files the app writes; (d) `ScanColumnUnit` = `DegreeColumnUnit` | `RadianColumnUnit` | `NanometerColumnUnit` | `MicrometerColumnUnit` | `ElectronVoltColumnUnit` | `WavenumberColumnUnit`, the unit a scan column's numbers are in, texts `°`, `rad`, `nm`, `µm`, `eV` and `cm⁻¹`, with `member this.spectralUnitOpt : Units.UnitOfMeasure option` answering `Nanometer`, `Micrometer`, `ElectronVolt` and `Wavenumber` (`Units.fs:UnitOfMeasure`) for the four spectral cases and `None` for the two angle cases; (e) `ScanReading` = `RawDialReading` | `PhysicalScanValue`, whether a scan column holds the reading on an item's dial or the physical value (001 §I 'experiments record raw dial readings'), texts `raw dial reading` and `physical value`. (3) After them, `DataColumnNumber of int` with `.value`, a column of a lab file counted from 1: `static member tryCreate (number : int) : DataColumnNumber option` answers `None` below 1, and `member this.index : int` is `value - 1`, its position among a row's cells. No other type, member or option is added. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs`: `CanonicalJson.options` gains one converter each for `DataDelimiter`, `HeaderRowChoice`, `ByteOrderMark`, `ScanColumnUnit` and `ScanReading`, written as step 166's `KitStar` converter is and registered with the others before the `JsonFSharpConverter`: each writes the case's `value` and reads through its `tryOfWire`, an unknown tag throwing `JsonException`, which the callers report as `MalformedJsonErr`. Nothing else in the options changes. Tests. `KitTests` (step 122) gains `the closed sets of an import profile round-trip their disk tags and render their texts`: for each of the five unions, `tryOfWire` of each case's `value` answers the case, the tags run 1 to n in `all`'s order, 0 and n + 1 answer `None`, and the texts are exactly as above; `CommaDelimiter.character` is `,` and `TabDelimiter.character` the tab character; `NanometerColumnUnit.spectralUnitOpt` is `Some Nanometer` and `RadianColumnUnit.spectralUnitOpt` is `None`; `DataColumnNumber.tryCreate 0` is `None` and `(DataColumnNumber 3).index` is 2; and `ImportProfileName.builtIns` holds `Intensity series`, `Ellipsometric series`, `Phone ROI CSV` and `Mueller-matrix observations`, in that order. In `CanonicalJsonTests` (steps 28, 166, 285), `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` also writes `SemicolonDelimiter` as `2`, `NoHeaderRow` as `2`, `ByteOrderMarkPresent` as `1`, `WavenumberColumnUnit` as `6` and `RawDialReading` as `1`, each read back equal, and `an unknown disk tag is refused` also refuses the `DataDelimiter` tag `4` and the `ScanColumnUnit` tag `7` as it refuses the others.

**Acceptance.** After the profile's closed sets land, `DataDelimiter`, `HeaderRowChoice`, `ByteOrderMark`, `ScanColumnUnit` and `ScanReading` MUST carry 1-based int disk tags read back by `tryOfWire` and written by `CanonicalJson.options` as those tags, `DataColumnNumber` MUST count from 1, and `ImportProfileName.builtIns` MUST name the four built-in profiles; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the closed sets of an import profile round-trip their disk tags and render their texts`, the count rising by 1, and the changed `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` and `an unknown disk tag is refused`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.
